{
  "summary": "Enables running the transaction index (-txindex) alongside block pruning (-prune), provided the index does not contain pre-v32 legacy entries. When a transaction lookup targets a pruned block, GetTransaction, REST, and RPC interfaces return the candidate block hashes instead of a generic not-found error. Callers can then download the missing blocks on demand via getblockfrompeer and retry, while getrawtransaction at verbosity 2 gracefully omits fee and prevout fields when undo data is absent.",
  "problem": "Nodes running in pruned mode cannot enable -txindex, forcing users who need raw transaction lookups, proof generation, or PSBT input resolution to maintain an unpruned node with hundreds of gigabytes of disk space.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description notes it resolves four long-standing issues requesting txindex support on pruned nodes: #10609 (opened in 2017), #12651, #16182, and #35240.",
    "Builds on merged PR #35531, which restructured txindex records to map transactions to block hashes rather than direct disk file offsets."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Adds an optional data field to JSONRPCError, introduces src/node/tx_lookup_result.h, and changes the return type of node::GetTransaction from CTransactionRef to TxLookupResult.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Added a dedicated release note file (doc/release-notes-36002.md) and expanded test coverage for block undo data handling.",
  "card": "Allows Bitcoin Core nodes to run txindex concurrently with block pruning if the index contains no legacy file-offset entries. When looking up a transaction in a pruned block, txindex lookups surface the missing block hashes via REST and JSON-RPC error responses so callers can fetch them using getblockfrompeer and retry. Additionally, getrawtransaction at verbosity 2 omits fee and prevout data instead of failing when undo data is missing for refetched blocks. This addresses four issues dating back to 2017 (#10609, #12651, #16182, #35240) requesting pruned txindex functionality.",
